Describe the JavaScript event loop, distinguishing between macro‑tasks and micro‑tasks. Then, given the code snippet below, explain the order of console logs and why a <code>setTimeout</code> callback runs after a resolved <code>Promise</code>:
<pre>
console.log('A');
setTimeout(() => console.log('B'), 0);
Promise.resolve().then(() => console.log('C'));
console.log('D');
</pre>
